      "id": 1,
      "text": "Newdale Colony was established in 1993 after dividing from the Hillside Hutterite Colony in Spink County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/newdale_colony_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Newdale Colony is part of the Schmiedeleut Group 1, emphasizing shared property and communal labor in agricultural pursuits.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/newdale_colony_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The surrounding terrain of Newdale Colony consists of flat to gently rolling prairie landforms typical of the Coteau des Prairies region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/newdale_colony_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Newdale Colony experiences a humid continental climate with cold, snowy winters and warm summers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/newdale_colony_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Extensive grain and livestock farming dominate the prairie ecosystem surrounding Newdale Colony.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
